<br/>
<h2>Top Stories</h2><br/>
<h3>'iPhone Ultra' Likely to 'Repeat the iPhone X Story' With Delayed Launch</h3><br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/05/foldable-iphone-to-repeat-iphone-x-story/">Apple will likely "repeat the iPhone X story"</a> by unveiling its foldable iPhone at the same time as the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max, but starting foldable iPhone pre-orders at a later date, according to analyst Ming-Chi Kuo.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2022/09/iPhone-X-2022-Upload.jpg" alt="" width="1142" height="644" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-863523" /><br/>
Kuo this week said manufacturing challenges have limited early production of the foldable iPhone, which will reportedly be named iPhone Ultra. As a result, he believes the device may launch at some point after the iPhone 18 Pro models.<br/>
<br/>
In 2017, Apple unveiled the iPhone 8, iPhone 8 Plus, and iPhone X on September 12. iPhone 8 and iPhone 8 Plus pre-orders began just three days later, while iPhone X pre-orders began six weeks later on Friday, October 27. Likewise, Kuo believes the foldable iPhone may not be available to pre-order until the fourth quarter of 2026.<br/>
<br/>
